---
pre-compare: sort
---

// Synthetic PAN-OS records; every value is invented. The column order follows
// the PAN-OS 11.1 Traffic, URL Filtering (125 columns), and Threat log fields.
// https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/traffic-log-fields
// https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/url-filtering-log-fields
// https://docs.paloaltonetworks.com/ngfw/administration/monitoring/use-syslog-for-monitoring/syslog-field-descriptions/threat-log-fields
// Device-ID operating systems and device categories and VM UUIDs become
// endpoint details, the HTTP status code and content type the HTTP response,
// and the threat category and the email of a WildFire record the finding types
// and email evidence.
from_file env("TENZIR_INPUT") {
  read_lines
}
this = line.parse_syslog()
paloalto::ocsf::normalize
this = ocsf_cast(ocsf_derive(this))
this = {
  sequence: metadata.sequence,
  src_endpoint: src_endpoint?,
  dst_endpoint: dst_endpoint?,
  http_response: http_response?,
  finding_types: finding_info?.types?,
  email: evidences?[0]?.email?,
  unmapped: unmapped,
}
drop_null_fields
